{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":248525,"num_turns":12,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"add6cb7e-9b8f-4302-be69-924ee7d0bd98","total_cost_usd":1.0681455,"usage":{"input_tokens":3663,"cache_creation_input_tokens":51326,"cache_read_input_tokens":156179,"output_tokens":18299,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":51326,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1158,"cache_read_input_tokens":49564,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1762,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1762},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":921,"outputTokens":17,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.001006,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-4-8":{"inputTokens":3663,"outputTokens":18299,"cacheReadInputTokens":156179,"cacheCreationInputTokens":51326,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.0671395,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-4-8","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The implementation is in place. Here's a summary.\n\n## Behavior changed\n\nI rewrote `_best_play_index` (the helper behind step 4 \"Develop the board\" in `_choose_main`) and added four small helpers. This is the only decision point touched; attack, evolve, and Energy-transfer logic are unchanged.\n\n**Before:** among playable Basic Pokémon, the strongest by `_card_power` was benched first.\n\n**After:** playable Basics are ranked by a primary *Grass core Bench role* key, then `_card_power` as tiebreak. Roles, highest first: **Yanma** (Yanmega relay) → **Chikorita** (Meganium 710) → **Bulbasaur** (Mega Venusaur) → **Teal Mask Ogerpon ex** (only when Grass Energy is available). A role already represented on the board at *any* evolution stage drops back to ordinary support ranking, so a redundant second copy never outranks a still-missing core role — implementing both \"prioritize missing roles\" and \"avoid redundant support blocking those roles.\"\n\nSupporting helpers: `_card_role` (name-based with card-ID fallback), `_roles_in_play`, `_in_play_mons`, `_grass_energy_available` (checks attached-in-play or in-hand Basic Energy; the deck's only Basic Energy is Grass, id 1).\n\n**Scope/propagation:** Because `SEARCH_MAIN` lookahead decides the top-level MAIN action by rolling out greedily, this ordering changes real behavior mainly when Bench slots are contended (the exact case the strategy cares about) — the greedy rollout tail now benches core roles before support, so `_eval_state` sees different end-of-turn boards. It also directly governs the greedy fallback path. Kaggle contract preserved: still self-contained, still defines `agent(obs_dict)` and `read_deck_csv()`, no new imports/deps.\n\n## Concerns for the human reviewer\n\n1. **`card.name` dependency (primary):** Chikorita-vs-Bulbasaur ordering relies on `getattr(card, \"name\", \"\")`. If the `cg` Card model has no `name` attribute, the two 4-copy basics (917/918) can't be told apart, and only Yanma/Ogerpon (and the evolution-stage presence checks via `_ROLE_BY_ID`) still fire — the mechanism partially degrades to a no-op for those two roles rather than crashing. Worth confirming `name` exists, and that 917/918 map to Chikorita/Bulbasaur as assumed.\n2. **`me.hand` visibility:** the Ogerpon Grass-Energy gate reads `getattr(me, \"hand\", None)`; if own-hand contents aren't exposed, it falls back to attached-in-play Grass Energy only (still correct, just more conservative).\n3. **Second-copy simplification:** a redundant copy is demoted to ordinary ranking rather than fully suppressed, so the strategy's \"second Yanma when first is threatened/prized\" nuance isn't modeled — it can still be benched if it's the best remaining play.\n4. As with any MAIN-play change, this should get trace evidence showing the role priority actually fires (the prior EXP-0003 was rejected partly for lacking such a trace), plus a cross-check that it doesn't regress on the standard opponents.\n\nI did not run benchmarks or touch `deck.csv`, `context/`, or any parent-directory files, per the contract.","ttft_ms":1692,"ttft_stream_ms":1544,"time_to_request_ms":35,"type":"result","duration_ms":247698,"uuid":"26bd9ae7-2ec5-447c-a414-1dc7a6203a2d"}
